WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.935
-My first guest is
a talented comedian

00:00:02.935 --> 00:00:05.238
and the host of
"The Daily Show."

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:08.942
Tickets to see him live on the
"Back to Abnormal" tour

00:00:08.942 --> 00:00:11.877
are available at trevornoah.com.

00:00:11.877 --> 00:00:14.914
Ladies and gentlemen,
please welcome Trevor Noah!

00:00:14.914 --> 00:00:15.948
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:15.948 --> 00:00:17.684
-♪ Trevor Noah ♪

00:00:17.684 --> 00:00:20.019
♪ Back another time ♪

00:00:20.019 --> 00:00:21.587
♪ Cannot arrest him ♪

00:00:21.587 --> 00:00:24.290
♪ Even though
he was born a crime ♪

00:00:25.792 --> 00:00:27.460
♪ Now he got to know ♪

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:29.862
♪ He sees it ♪

00:00:29.862 --> 00:00:32.632
♪ On "The Daily Show," yeah ♪

00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:34.367
-Trevor Noah!

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:37.337
-Oh, yeah!
-Oh, look at that.

00:00:37.337 --> 00:00:38.805
How does that feel?
-Wow!

00:00:38.805 --> 00:00:40.673
-That's got to feel good, huh?
-Wow!

00:00:40.673 --> 00:00:43.343
-Come out to a standing "O"?
Come on. They love you, man.

00:00:43.343 --> 00:00:45.177
-It's a little --
It's a little overwhelming.

00:00:45.177 --> 00:00:47.380
[ Cheers and applause ]
It's wonderful. Thank you.

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:48.381
But it's a little --
It's a little overwhelming.

00:00:48.381 --> 00:00:49.749
-It is, right?

00:00:49.749 --> 00:00:52.485
-I've been small for very long.
-I know. You really have.

00:00:52.485 --> 00:00:53.520
-You know what
I feel like is happening

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:54.720
right now with the pandemic?

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:57.623
I almost feel like, you know,
the dinosaurs

00:00:57.623 --> 00:00:59.392
probably thought about,
like, the world like this,

00:00:59.392 --> 00:01:00.960
like, when the asteroid hits.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.728
And they were like, "Boom,"
and then they were like, "Whoa!"

00:01:02.728 --> 00:01:04.230
And then they were
like, "Oh, we survived."

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:06.732
And they were like,
"Let's carry on with our lives."

00:01:06.732 --> 00:01:08.734
Let's go to 'The Tonight Show.'"
-Yeah.

00:01:08.734 --> 00:01:10.937
-And then the cloud came,
and they were like, "Oh, man.

00:01:10.937 --> 00:01:12.705
We got confident too quickly."

00:01:12.705 --> 00:01:14.107
-I know.
-I don't know. I don't know.

00:01:14.107 --> 00:01:15.708
-I feel like
we're on the baby steps --

00:01:15.708 --> 00:01:16.909
-And I hope so.

00:01:16.909 --> 00:01:18.912
I hope -- Baby steps in
the right direction.

00:01:18.912 --> 00:01:20.646
Either way, we're having fun
along the way.

00:01:20.646 --> 00:01:22.582
-We're having fun.
-Yeah.

00:01:22.582 --> 00:01:24.417
-We're getting back to
wearing masks.

00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:26.552
We're doing the right thing.
-You know what my thing is, man?

00:01:26.552 --> 00:01:28.554
I go like, "This is what
the vaccine is supposed to be."

00:01:28.554 --> 00:01:29.755
I was like, "I got the vaccine"

00:01:29.755 --> 00:01:31.791
and I was like,
"I'm now going to have fun."

00:01:31.791 --> 00:01:33.292
So I was like,
"I'm going to test the vaccine."

00:01:33.292 --> 00:01:34.426
First place I went to,
I went to Miami.

00:01:34.426 --> 00:01:35.495
That was the first thing I did.

00:01:35.495 --> 00:01:37.230
I was like,
"I've got the vaccine."

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:38.464
I was like,
"I'm going to go Miami,

00:01:38.464 --> 00:01:40.033
because I want to see if
the vaccine works."

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:42.201
And I went to Miami, and --
-You tested it out.

00:01:42.201 --> 00:01:43.369
-That was great.
Didn't get COVID.

00:01:43.369 --> 00:01:45.638
Got other diseases,
but didn't get COVID.

00:01:45.638 --> 00:01:48.274
[ Cheers and applause ]
-That's Miami, yeah.

00:01:48.274 --> 00:01:50.009
-Yeah.
-That's right.

00:01:50.009 --> 00:01:51.578
-But it's good to be back, man.

00:01:51.578 --> 00:01:53.813
-I am happy and thankful
that you're back here,

00:01:53.813 --> 00:01:55.981
because, you know,
I saw that you did

00:01:55.981 --> 00:01:58.016
stand-up over the summer for
the first time, 'cause --

00:01:58.016 --> 00:01:59.218
-Yeah, it was crazy, man.

00:01:59.218 --> 00:02:00.686
-Because I've been
watching your show.

00:02:00.686 --> 00:02:03.589
It's been great, but it's been
you in a corner of your house.

00:02:03.589 --> 00:02:05.524
-Yes. It sounds
very depressing, doesn't it?

00:02:05.524 --> 00:02:08.127
-But it's very funny.
It's very funny.

00:02:08.127 --> 00:02:09.662
And I watch it and then I go,

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:11.164
"Oh, you went out and
did stand-up."

00:02:11.164 --> 00:02:12.765
And I go -- When did you decide,

00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:13.966
"Oh, I'm doing --
I have to go out and do --"

00:02:13.966 --> 00:02:15.267
-I didn't decide.

00:02:15.267 --> 00:02:18.237
So, what happened was,
no comedian really decided.

00:02:18.237 --> 00:02:20.874
So, Dave Chappelle
decided, right?

00:02:20.874 --> 00:02:23.309
He was like, "I'm doing comedy."

00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:25.077
And then he started phoning
people and he's like,

00:02:25.077 --> 00:02:26.713
"You're doing comedy."

00:02:26.713 --> 00:02:28.214
And I was like,
"No, I'm staying at home."

00:02:28.214 --> 00:02:30.450
And he's like, "No, you're not."

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:32.718
And then he, like,
started doing comedy in, like,

00:02:32.718 --> 00:02:34.787
a cornfield in Ohio.

00:02:34.787 --> 00:02:35.855
-That's correct.

00:02:35.855 --> 00:02:37.423
-Which I thought was,
like, a joke.

00:02:37.423 --> 00:02:38.524
Like, even when he said it,
I was like, "Ha!

00:02:38.524 --> 00:02:39.558
That's a nice concept."

00:02:39.558 --> 00:02:41.060
And he's like,
"No, I'm being serious."

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:42.194
And then I got there,
and it was an actual --

00:02:42.194 --> 00:02:43.496
I thought it was like --

00:02:43.496 --> 00:02:45.131
You know when people say
things -- "It's in a field" --

00:02:45.131 --> 00:02:47.200
you think it, like,
it just means in an open --

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:49.334
No, it was a field.
-You were in a field.

00:02:49.334 --> 00:02:50.436
-Just driving in Ohio.

00:02:50.436 --> 00:02:52.237
It was like farm, farm,
cow, cow, cow,

00:02:52.237 --> 00:02:54.440
farm, farm, corn, corn, corn,
Dave Chappelle.

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:55.841
-Wow.

00:02:55.841 --> 00:02:58.444
-And then it was just like
we're doing comedy in a field.

00:02:58.444 --> 00:03:01.281
And then, every time, he would
pop up, and he'd just be like,

00:03:01.281 --> 00:03:02.415
"You're doing comedy again."

00:03:02.415 --> 00:03:03.683
And then I would just
do the comedy.

00:03:03.683 --> 00:03:05.451
So I didn't really decide --
And I'm grateful to him,

00:03:05.451 --> 00:03:08.220
because, like, I think a lot of
comedians needed one comedian

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:09.355
to be like, "Poke, poke.

00:03:09.355 --> 00:03:11.190
You're going.
You're gonna do the show."

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:13.793
-And did you have a little bit
of an act in your head

00:03:13.793 --> 00:03:14.793
or you just go, like -- No.

00:03:14.793 --> 00:03:17.229
-I mean, it's been crazy, like,

00:03:17.229 --> 00:03:18.664
because you don't see
the people.

00:03:18.664 --> 00:03:19.665
Do you know what I mean?

00:03:19.665 --> 00:03:20.966
And then,
when you see the people --

00:03:20.966 --> 00:03:23.036
Like, because the masks are on,
and you don't know

00:03:23.036 --> 00:03:25.171
what's happening
behind anybody's faces.

00:03:25.171 --> 00:03:26.539
-That's true.

00:03:26.539 --> 00:03:28.140
-And, like, our whole lives,
we've been told that masks

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:29.642
are, like, the bad guy.

00:03:29.642 --> 00:03:31.243
Bad guys wear masks.
You know what I mean?

00:03:31.243 --> 00:03:32.945
Now it's like --
Now good guys wear masks.

00:03:32.945 --> 00:03:34.280
You know what I mean?

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:35.715
-It's the opposite of
anything --

00:03:35.715 --> 00:03:37.350
-Yeah, it's like the complete
opposite of everything now.

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:38.618
And now you don't know
if people are smiling.

00:03:38.618 --> 00:03:40.853
So, like, everyone has
to do, like, extra work.

00:03:40.853 --> 00:03:42.855
[ Laughter ]

00:03:42.855 --> 00:03:45.557
-There's a lot of eye work.
-"I'm very happy to see you!"

00:03:45.557 --> 00:03:47.126
-Yeah, a lot of eye work.

00:03:47.126 --> 00:03:49.195
I got a picture of you
out that night,

00:03:49.195 --> 00:03:52.030
and here's you, Chris Rock,
and Dave Chappelle.

00:03:52.030 --> 00:03:53.633
-That was wild, man.
-I mean --

00:03:53.633 --> 00:03:57.103
-That was -- But you see,
this is -- So, this is where --

00:03:57.103 --> 00:03:58.638
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:58.638 --> 00:04:01.407
This is where
I actually got tricked.

00:04:01.407 --> 00:04:03.776
So, Dave said he was
doing a show

00:04:03.776 --> 00:04:05.478
that I should come and watch.

00:04:05.478 --> 00:04:07.179
And, so, I rode
a sissy bike there.

00:04:07.179 --> 00:04:09.749
That's how confident I was that
I wasn't performing, right?

00:04:09.749 --> 00:04:11.317
Because you don't ride a bicycle

00:04:11.317 --> 00:04:13.252
when you're going to,
like, perform at a show.

00:04:13.252 --> 00:04:14.854
That's, like -- As a comedian --
Because the thing is,

00:04:14.854 --> 00:04:16.022
if you go to a show, you don't
know if it's going to go

00:04:16.022 --> 00:04:17.790
well or if it's
going to go badly, right?

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:18.958
And so if it goes badly,

00:04:18.958 --> 00:04:20.025
you don't want to be
riding a bicycle home.

00:04:20.025 --> 00:04:21.260
-No, it's very sad.

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:24.931
That's the most depressing
thing in the world.

00:04:24.931 --> 00:04:26.065
-You just want to be
in, like, the back of a car

00:04:26.065 --> 00:04:27.166
being like, "That was terrible."

00:04:27.166 --> 00:04:28.334
You don't want to ride
a bicycle home.

00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:29.535
-No.
-So I rode a bicycle there.

00:04:29.535 --> 00:04:30.836
And then he was like,
"Oh, you're performing."

00:04:30.836 --> 00:04:32.738
And then I was like, "But I rode
a bicycle here, Dave."

00:04:32.738 --> 00:04:36.275
Like, "I can't bomb
and then ride my bike home."

00:04:36.275 --> 00:04:37.510
-But, yeah, again,
it was amazing.

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:39.178
I mean, it's Dave Chappelle
and Chris Rock,

00:04:39.178 --> 00:04:40.679
and the three of us are onstage

00:04:40.679 --> 00:04:42.515
and we're working material
and we're trying,

00:04:42.515 --> 00:04:44.984
and the audience was so happy
to be out again.

00:04:44.984 --> 00:04:47.619
It was just, yeah, it was --
Those are dream moments in life.

00:04:47.619 --> 00:04:50.823
-Everyone must ask,
but do you get advice from

00:04:50.823 --> 00:04:51.890
Dave Chappelle or Chris Rock?

00:04:51.890 --> 00:04:53.025
-Oh, yeah, definitely.

00:04:53.025 --> 00:04:56.095
If you just listen to them,
it's advice.

00:04:56.095 --> 00:04:57.997
You know, like Chris Rock --
I used to work

00:04:57.997 --> 00:04:59.665
seven days a week,
and I was, like, proud of it.

00:04:59.665 --> 00:05:00.766
I was like,
"I work seven days a week.

00:05:00.766 --> 00:05:02.301
I work seven days a week,
every day."

00:05:02.301 --> 00:05:03.369
And then Chris Rock was like,
"You're going to be

00:05:03.369 --> 00:05:06.872
the most unfunny comedian
of all time."

00:05:06.872 --> 00:05:08.073
And I was like, "What?"

00:05:08.073 --> 00:05:09.642
And he's like,
"You work all the time."

00:05:09.642 --> 00:05:11.511
He's like, "Comedy comes
from life, you know?"

00:05:11.511 --> 00:05:12.678
And he was like,
"If you work every day,

00:05:12.678 --> 00:05:13.979
what is your comedy gonna --

00:05:13.979 --> 00:05:16.549
Your comedy is going to start
being about comedy."

00:05:16.549 --> 00:05:18.718
And I was like, "Oh, man.
I never thought about that."

00:05:18.718 --> 00:05:19.819
-That's wild.
-Yeah.

00:05:19.819 --> 00:05:21.754
And, like,
he's told me so many things.

00:05:21.754 --> 00:05:23.122
Chappelle has given me advice.

00:05:23.122 --> 00:05:24.891
Chappelle will
give me advice, though.

00:05:24.891 --> 00:05:26.926
He'll go,
"Here's all the advice,"

00:05:26.926 --> 00:05:28.727
and then, at the end of it,
he goes,

00:05:28.727 --> 00:05:31.431
"But don't take my advice,
'cause, I mean..."

00:05:31.431 --> 00:05:32.831
-That's interesting, right?

00:05:32.831 --> 00:05:34.233
And then,
"Don't take my advice."

00:05:34.233 --> 00:05:35.934
-Yeah, his advice is always
like, "Don't listen to me."

00:05:35.934 --> 00:05:38.671
-But you did have some time off.
-I did, man.

00:05:38.671 --> 00:05:41.007
I tried to use it as much --
I tell everybody,

00:05:41.007 --> 00:05:43.276
man, we don't know what life

00:05:43.276 --> 00:05:45.010
is going to be like
or not be like,

00:05:45.010 --> 00:05:48.013
so use the little opportunities
that you get

00:05:48.013 --> 00:05:49.514
to just live a little bit more,

00:05:49.514 --> 00:05:50.783
you know,
even if it means walk--

00:05:50.783 --> 00:05:53.586
I've walked in more parks in
New York than I ever did

00:05:53.586 --> 00:05:55.087
in like the six years
since I moved here.

00:05:55.087 --> 00:05:57.590
Now I'm like, "There's a park."
I walk in it.

00:05:57.590 --> 00:05:58.591
-Yeah.
-You know what I mean?

00:05:58.591 --> 00:06:00.459
Before, I was like,
"Ew, a park.

00:06:00.459 --> 00:06:01.861
Why am I taking the park?"

00:06:01.861 --> 00:06:03.595
Now I --
Like, I do touristy things.

00:06:03.595 --> 00:06:04.730
You know how many people
live in the city,

00:06:04.730 --> 00:06:06.498
and they've never seen
any of the sights?

00:06:06.498 --> 00:06:07.833
-No.
-We take it for granted.

00:06:07.833 --> 00:06:09.201
-We really do, yeah.

00:06:09.201 --> 00:06:11.871
People go like, "Do you go see
the Statue of Liberty?"

00:06:11.871 --> 00:06:13.906
I'm like, "No.
I don't see that every day.

00:06:13.906 --> 00:06:15.841
I know it exists. It's here."
-You see?

00:06:15.841 --> 00:06:16.975
And that's what
I'm talking about.

00:06:16.975 --> 00:06:19.712
So I've tried to just, like,
live a bit more.

00:06:19.712 --> 00:06:22.147
And that's what I'm been doing
during this period,

00:06:22.147 --> 00:06:24.049
just, like, trying to live
a little it more,

00:06:24.049 --> 00:06:26.051
to appreciate
what we didn't have.

00:06:26.051 --> 00:06:28.954
-You're doing your
"Back to Abnormal" Tour,

00:06:28.954 --> 00:06:30.923
which is --
You're gonna be in London.

00:06:30.923 --> 00:06:32.191
You're going all over.
-Yes.

00:06:32.191 --> 00:06:35.561
I'm going to London tonight,
and then start the show.

00:06:35.561 --> 00:06:37.196
So, it's going to be at
the O2 Arena.

00:06:37.196 --> 00:06:38.664
Really excited. It's sold out.
-Wow!

00:06:38.664 --> 00:06:41.667
-And, yeah, I mean, like,
the U.K. is just open.

00:06:41.667 --> 00:06:43.935
That's how -- That's, like --
I love how every country

00:06:43.935 --> 00:06:45.070
is just going with
their own thing.

00:06:45.070 --> 00:06:46.172
Do you know what I mean?

00:06:46.172 --> 00:06:47.340
No, because, like,
Americans are like,

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:49.575
"Alright, look, guys,
we're sort of open,

00:06:49.575 --> 00:06:51.210
but we're not open fully."

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:52.211
And then, in the U.K.,
they were like,

00:06:52.211 --> 00:06:53.379
"We're closed, we're closed,

00:06:53.379 --> 00:06:54.480
we're closed, we're closed.
we're closed."

00:06:54.480 --> 00:06:55.514
Then they're like,
"Alright, it's open.

00:06:55.514 --> 00:06:56.515
We don't care anymore.
We're open.

00:06:56.515 --> 00:06:58.216
It's all open.
It's all open.

00:06:58.216 --> 00:07:00.619
This is how it's gonna be now.
We're all open.

00:07:00.619 --> 00:07:02.221
This is what we're doing.

00:07:02.221 --> 00:07:04.956
-And "Daily Show" comes back --
-Yeah.

00:07:04.956 --> 00:07:07.426
-When are you back?
-Next week, Monday, we're back.

00:07:07.426 --> 00:07:10.662
-Next Monday, you're back.
-Yeah. We're back next Monday.

00:07:10.662 --> 00:07:14.233
-I think the show that you were
doing was amazing, by the way.

00:07:14.233 --> 00:07:16.569
You did great work
when we needed you.

00:07:16.569 --> 00:07:17.569
We needed people to
come out and entertain,

00:07:17.569 --> 00:07:18.871
and you were right there.

00:07:18.871 --> 00:07:20.873
And you were like, "Yep,
I got to do it from my house.

00:07:20.873 --> 00:07:22.074
I'm going to do it,"
and you just did it.

00:07:22.074 --> 00:07:23.475
I thought that was awesome.
-Thank you, man.

00:07:23.475 --> 00:07:25.244
-Props to you for doing that.
-I had a lot of fun. Yeah.

00:07:25.244 --> 00:07:27.746
-You got creative
and really good.

00:07:27.746 --> 00:07:30.616
But now, are you
gonna go back to the suits?

00:07:30.616 --> 00:07:32.884
-Well, we can't go back
anywhere right now

00:07:32.884 --> 00:07:34.319
because we're in
the middle of --

00:07:34.319 --> 00:07:36.522
So it's like, "Are we going to
try find a space --"

00:07:36.522 --> 00:07:38.657
I think my neighbors
are happy, you know?

00:07:38.657 --> 00:07:39.958
Because, like,
my neighbors were like,

00:07:39.958 --> 00:07:41.927
"So, this is, like, where you
make the show now?"

00:07:41.927 --> 00:07:43.762
I'm like, "Yeah.
This is me making the show."

00:07:43.762 --> 00:07:46.365
I'm just, like, the guy
screaming next door to you,

00:07:46.365 --> 00:07:48.233
"Welcome back!"

00:07:48.233 --> 00:07:49.502
-Crazy -- Yeah.

00:07:49.502 --> 00:07:50.636
-The neighbors were just like,
"Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:07:50.636 --> 00:07:51.938
No, you can go."

00:07:51.938 --> 00:07:53.205
So, yeah, I'm figuring out
the pieces now.

00:07:53.205 --> 00:07:54.640
It's going to be exciting.

00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:57.710
Like, I'm trying new things.
I'm playing -- You know what?

00:07:57.710 --> 00:07:59.611
I think what COVID
has done to me is,

00:07:59.611 --> 00:08:04.049
it's made me a little
bit less afraid to fail in life,

00:08:04.049 --> 00:08:06.418
because when COVID happened,
it took everything away from us.

00:08:06.418 --> 00:08:07.787
Do you know what I mean?

00:08:07.787 --> 00:08:10.456
It took away our friends.
It took away our opportunities.

00:08:10.456 --> 00:08:11.958
It took away
so many people's jobs.

00:08:11.958 --> 00:08:14.326
It took away dreams.
It took away aspirations.

00:08:14.326 --> 00:08:18.396
And so now I feel ungrateful
not trying to live life

00:08:18.396 --> 00:08:21.066
a little bit more because there
is life to be lived.

00:08:21.066 --> 00:08:22.267
Does that make sense?
-Yeah, absolutely.

00:08:22.267 --> 00:08:23.869
-Yeah, so now I'm just like --
-I love that.

00:08:23.869 --> 00:08:24.936
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:24.936 --> 00:08:26.405
-Have fun.
-I love that.

00:08:26.405 --> 00:08:27.539
-Try it.
-We're going to have fun.

00:08:27.539 --> 00:08:29.174
When we come back,
more with Trevor Noah.

00:08:29.174 --> 00:08:30.209
Come on back.

